ition (U) at least one line must be non\u2011sunny; therefore a configuration with \\(n\\) sunny lines cannot exist.\n\n6. **Conclusion**  \n   The admissible numbers of sunny lines are precisely  \n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{\\{0,1,2,\\dots ,\\,n-1\\}} .\n   \\]\n\n   Both the upper bound and the constructive realizations for every admissible \\(k\\) have been proved rigorously."
